       - Fuse the scaling by beta with the rank-k update, so each
         C[i][j] is loaded and stored exactly once.
       - Change the inner loop to iterate over k (columns of A),
         turning accesses A[i][k] and A[j][k] into contiguous
         row-wise traversals, which significantly improves cache
         locality compared to the original k-outer, j-inner order.
       - Accumulate the result in a scalar register (cij) to reduce
         repeated memory traffic and enable better vectorization.
     The iteration order of k for each fixed (i,j) is unchanged
     (0 .. m-1), so the floating-point accumulation order per output
     element is preserved. */
  for (i = 0; i < _PB_N; i++) {
    DATA_TYPE *Ci = C_[i];        /* Row i of C */
    const DATA_TYPE *Ai = A_[i];  /* Row i of A */

